==================================================================
DAY 48 - PART B: LAB
Watch pods and then nodes scale out and back in
Time: 90-120 minutes
==================================================================

STEP 1: Cluster and metrics-server
----------------------------------
cd ~/k8s-journey/cloud/eks && eksctl create cluster -f cluster.yaml
k apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml
k rollout status deploy/metrics-server -n kube-system
sleep 60 ; k top nodes
(You can also install it as an EKS add-on: eksctl create addon --cluster lab --name metrics-server)


STEP 2: CPU-heavy app with requests
-----------------------------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/cloud/eks/autoscale && cd $_
vi php-apache.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: php-apache
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels: {run: php-apache}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {run: php-apache}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: php-apache
        image: registry.k8s.io/hpa-example
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 200m
          limits:
            cpu: 500m
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: php-apache
spec:
  selector: {run: php-apache}
  ports:
  - port: 80

k apply -f php-apache.yaml


STEP 3: Create the HPA
----------------------
k autoscale deploy php-apache --cpu-percent=50 --min=1 --max=20
k get hpa php-apache -o yaml > hpa.yaml     # keep the YAML
k get hpa


STEP 4: Generate load
---------------------
Terminal 2: k get hpa php-apache -w
Terminal 3: k get pods -l run=php-apache -w
Terminal 1:
  for n in load load2 load3; do
    k run $n --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c "while true; do wget -q -O- http://php-apache >/dev/null; done"
  done

Watch TARGETS climb (e.g. 250%/50%) and REPLICAS increase.


STEP 5: Pods go Pending -> install Cluster Autoscaler
-----------------------------------------------------
With maxReplicas 20 x 200m = 4 CPU, 2 t3.medium nodes run out.
  k get pods -l run=php-apache | grep -c Pending

helm repo add autoscaler https://kubernetes.github.io/autoscaler && helm repo update
helm install cluster-autoscaler autoscaler/cluster-autoscaler -n kube-system \
  --set autoDiscovery.clusterName=lab \
  --set awsRegion=ap-south-1 \
  --set extraArgs.balance-similar-node-groups=true \
  --set extraArgs.scale-down-unneeded-time=2m
k logs -n kube-system -l app.kubernetes.io/name=aws-cluster-autoscaler -f --tail=20

(EKS managed node groups are tagged for auto-discovery automatically;
the node role got autoscaling permissions from "autoScaler: true" in
cluster.yaml.)

Terminal 4: k get nodes -w
Within a few minutes the node group grows (up to maxSize 4), and
Pending pods start. Check the ASG in the EC2 console.


STEP 6: Scale back in
---------------------
k delete pod load load2 load3 --ignore-not-found
Watch: HPA reduces replicas after the ~5 min stabilization window;
then the Cluster Autoscaler removes unneeded nodes (we set 2m unneeded
time; default is 10m). Total ~10-15 minutes.
k get hpa ; k get nodes


STEP 7: Tune HPA behaviour (optional)
-------------------------------------
Edit hpa.yaml and add:
  behavior:
    scaleDown:
      stabilizationWindowSeconds: 60
      policies:
      - type: Percent
        value: 50
        periodSeconds: 30
    scaleUp:
      policies:
      - type: Pods
        value: 4
        periodSeconds: 15
k apply -f hpa.yaml and repeat the load test. Compare the timing.


STEP 8 (READ): Karpenter / Auto Mode / Spot
-------------------------------------------
Karpenter replaces CA: a NodePool defines allowed instance families,
capacity type (spot/on-demand), zones and limits; it launches right-
sized nodes in under a minute and consolidates. EKS Auto Mode enables
this without installing anything (cluster created with Auto Mode).
A Spot managed node group in eksctl:
  managedNodeGroups:
  - name: spot
    instanceTypes: [t3.medium, t3a.medium, t2.medium]
    spot: true
    minSize: 0
    maxSize: 5


STEP 9: CLEAN UP
----------------
helm uninstall cluster-autoscaler -n kube-system
k delete -f php-apache.yaml ; k delete hpa php-apache
eksctl delete cluster -f ~/k8s-journey/cloud/eks/cluster.yaml --wait


STEP 10: AKS / GKE equivalents
------------------------------
AKS: az aks update -g lab-rg -n lab --enable-cluster-autoscaler --min-count 1 --max-count 4
     (or Node Auto Provisioning, Karpenter-based)
GKE: gcloud container clusters update lab --enable-autoscaling --min-nodes 1
     --max-nodes 4 --node-pool default-pool --region asia-south1
     (Autopilot does node scaling for you)
HPA YAML is identical on all three.

cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day48: autoscaling"
